  // and named the path the OLD process had written:
  //   curl exit 22: curl: (22) The requested URL returned error: 500
  //     | body: could not open WAV input: /tmp/audiocpp-ui-1791356334209286/1-voy-doctor.wav
  // Those are the engine's own words, from src/framework/audio/wav_reader.cpp:412
  // (`throw std::runtime_error("could not open WAV input: " + path.string())`; :167 is the
  // same class with no path). It is not a capability answer (the payload is fine, the FILE is
  // not), not a busy answer, and not a socket death: the engine answered, in words, and what
