  // --- READ the tail of the lane log --------------------------------------------
  // The page log needed two fixes. The first was client-side persistence of the page log, and it is
  // built. This verb is the second. Before it the plugin only ever WROTE perf_log.jsonl: `perf_log`
  // was a toggle, and LogPane said out loud that it never fetches from the host, so "Log (recent
  // events)" was one page-instance's memory and not the lane's history at all.
  //
  // WHY A TAIL, NOT A READ. Measured 2026-10-12: perf_log.jsonl is 3 693 135 bytes. fsx.readBytes refuses
  // a file larger than its cap (FS_TOO_LARGE) instead of truncating it, so the honest read of a big log is
  // a byte window at the END: lstat for the size, readByteRange for the last window, and the first fragment
  // dropped when the window starts in the middle of a line. When lstat cannot report a size the window is
  // taken from the START and the answer says window:'from_start' — a reader has to be told which end it was
  // shown, because "the 25 oldest records in a 3.7 MB log" looks exactly like "the 25 newest".
  //
