        // SUPERSET of the plain one: text, then `segments`, then `speaker_turns`
        // (start_sample / end_sample / speaker_id / confidence / text), then `words`. The plain
        // route with response_format=text returns `text` alone, so a two-speaker render came back
        // as one unlabelled line even though the model had already done the speaker work - verified
        // live against ap-0289's moss_ttsd output, where the details route returned
        //   speaker 0 [0.00-1.34s] "Hello, how are you?"  /  speaker 1 [1.96-3.84s] "I am doing well, thank you."
        // The engine's own comment on write_transcript_detail_fields: a route that omits these
