          // Measured live on 2026-10-22, not in the mock: the policy names the root the command WRITES into. A move writes at BOTH ends — texts/presets/ (the file leaves) and texts-trash/ (the file lands) — so the root has to contain both. The first live run answered `mv exit 1` because this named only the source directory: the sandbox binds one workspaceRoot writable and the landing directory was outside it. BASE is the plugin's own storage dir, which is what writePolicy() defaults to, and the path gate above already keeps this command inside texts/.
